IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Internal Revenue Code of 1986 -- the one calendar computation of this encoding, kept in its own module because the daydate
-- library's overloaded arithmetic makes the stable l4 slow to check the larger modules that import it.
--
-- s 6013(b)(2)(A): a joint return after a separate return may not be made "after the expiration of 3 years from the last
-- date prescribed by law for filing the return for such taxable year (determined without regard to any extension of time
-- granted to either spouse)". That last date is set by s 6072, which is not deposited, so it is given.

§ `s 6013(b)(2)(A) -- the three years after the due date`

GIVEN `the due date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the s 6013(b)(2)(A) period from` `the due date` MEANS `add years` `the due date` 3

GIVEN `the due date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from the due date to the end of the s 6013(b)(2)(A) period` `the due date` MEANS
    Day (`the end of the s 6013(b)(2)(A) period from` `the due date`) MINUS Day `the due date`

-- A due date in the form the cases use, so that the case files need not import daydate.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS Date d m y
